  "lines": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "A union is like a harvest. You plant in spring and you do not eat the seed corn.",
      "emotion": "stern",
      "context_tags": [
        "quest_offer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "text": "Chicago thinks the food comes from a warehouse. It comes from dirt and rain.",
      "emotion": "stern",
      "context_tags": [
        "quest_offer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "text": "I have seen bad years. We are in one. We will plant through it.",
      "emotion": "stern",
      "context_tags": [
        "quest_offer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "text": "You want to know my plan? Same as every year. Work, store, share, repeat.",
      "emotion": "stern",
      "context_tags": [
        "quest_offer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "text": "The land does not care about your politics. It cares if you showed up.",
      "emotion": "stern",
      "context_tags": [
        "quest_offer"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
